Source measurements with missing timestamps within the existing HA history range and above the retention cutoff will be added. Existing Recorder rows are authoritative at exact timestamp conflicts. The gap policy applies only between the final imported prefix state and the first existing Recorder state; an artificial gap marker is not evidence of a CCU-Historian observation. If automatic purging is disabled, no retention cutoff applies. Older data will not be kept with auto_purge enabled. Verify your backup before confirming.

Verified CCU-Historian coverage: {coverage}. Only a complete, unchanged source query can be attested as continuous. CSV sources are excluded. Optional: select the complete-source confirmation only when the CCU-Historian series is genuinely complete. An import can proceed without requesting certification; synthetic transition markers prevent certification.

Daily supports are synthetic timestamps carrying only previously observed states from the selected source window, NOT measured midnight transitions or interpolated values. Supports must be inside Recorder retention, though a source observation before the cutoff may justify the first eligible midnight. No support is added where any observed state exists between 00:00 and 06:00. Generated supports cannot certify complete CCU-Historian coverage.

